      "origin_url": "https://www.gevernova.com/news/press-releases/ge-vernova-double-number-mit-interns-permanent-hires-2027",
      "published_at": "2026-10-06",
      "body_path": "docs/v4/stage4-corpus/round2/text/7d49d19fea0f5d6a7a91873b5c6177ed052b081efe89e008a49b979516a1b587.txt",
      "body_characters": 4597,
      "windows": [
        {
          "start": 2796,
          "end": 3330,
          "text": "Today's announcement reflects an urgent workforce reality outlined in GE Vernova's inaugural NextGen Workforce Study : the U.S. energy sector could need more than two million workers by 2032. To meet the massive growth in electricity demand driven by AI, data centers, and the industrial electrification surge, the study finds the industry will need one in every ten engineering graduates to join the power sector. GE Vernova's expanded MIT commitment is part of a broader effort to make those pathways visible and accessible earlier."
        }
      ],
      "full_document_review": false
    },
